<div class="ib-landing">

    <section class="ib-intro">
        <p>IB Computer Science is a two-year course in which students study how computer systems work, how software is designed, and how computational thinking is used to solve real problems. The course combines theory with practical problem-solving and programming, and is organised into two main areas: <strong>Concepts of computer science</strong> and <strong>Computational thinking and problem-solving</strong>. It is available at both Standard Level (SL) and Higher Level (HL).</p>
    </section>

    <section class="ib-section">
        <h2 class="ib-section-title">What You Study</h2>
        <p class="ib-section-intro">The course is split into two themes.</p>
    </section>

    {# ── Theme A ── #}
    <section class="ib-theme">
        <div class="ib-theme-header ib-theme-header--a">
            <h2 class="ib-theme-label">Theme A</h2>
            <p class="ib-theme-name">Concepts of Computer Science</p>
        </div>
        <p class="ib-theme-desc">This part of the course focuses on the theory behind computer systems, including how computers process data, how networks communicate, how databases are designed and queried, and how machine learning systems are developed and evaluated.</p>

        <div class="ib-unit-list">
            <a href="A1/index.html" class="ib-unit-card">
                <span class="ib-unit-code">A1</span>
                <div class="ib-unit-body">
                    <h3 class="ib-unit-name">Computer Fundamentals</h3>
                    <p class="ib-unit-desc">Core principles that underpin the operation of a computer system.</p>
                    <ul class="ib-subtopic-list">
                        <li>A1.1 Computer hardware and operation</li>
                        <li>A1.2 Data representation and computer logic</li>
                        <li>A1.3 Operating systems and control systems</li>
                        <li>A1.4 Translation <span class="ib-hl-badge">HL</span></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <span class="ib-unit-hours">SL: 11h | HL: 18h</span>
            </a>

            <a href="A2/index.html" class="ib-unit-card">
                <span class="ib-unit-code">A2</span>
                <div class="ib-unit-body">
                    <h3 class="ib-unit-name">Networks</h3>
                    <p class="ib-unit-desc">How computers communicate and how modern networks are structured and secured.</p>
                    <ul class="ib-subtopic-list">
                        <li>A2.1 Network fundamentals</li>
                        <li>A2.2 Network architecture</li>
                        <li>A2.3 Data transmissions</li>
                        <li>A2.4 Network security</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <span class="ib-unit-hours">SL: 11h | HL: 18h</span>
            </a>

            <a href="A3/index.html" class="ib-unit-card">
                <span class="ib-unit-code">A3</span>
                <div class="ib-unit-body">
                    <h3 class="ib-unit-name">Databases</h3>
                    <p class="ib-unit-desc">The storage, organisation and retrieval of data.</p>
                    <ul class="ib-subtopic-list">
                        <li>A3.1 Database fundamentals</li>
                        <li>A3.2 Database design</li>
                        <li>A3.3 Database programming</li>
                        <li>A3.4 Alternative databases and data warehouses <span class="ib-hl-badge">HL</span></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <span class="ib-unit-hours">SL: 11h | HL: 18h</span>
            </a>

            <a href="A4/index.html" class="ib-unit-card">
                <span class="ib-unit-code">A4</span>
                <div class="ib-unit-body">
                    <h3 class="ib-unit-name">Machine Learning</h3>
                    <p class="ib-unit-desc">Machine learning and some of the issues involved in building and using ML systems.</p>
                    <ul class="ib-subtopic-list">
                        <li>A4.1 Machine learning fundamentals</li>
                        <li>A4.2 Data preprocessing <span class="ib-hl-badge">HL</span></li>
                        <li>A4.3 Machine learning approaches <span class="ib-hl-badge">HL</span></li>
                        <li>A4.4 Ethical considerations</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <span class="ib-unit-hours">SL: 5h | HL: 18h</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── Theme B ── #}
    <section class="ib-theme">
        <div class="ib-theme-header ib-theme-header--b">
            <h2 class="ib-theme-label">Theme B</h2>
            <p class="ib-theme-name">Computational Thinking and Problem-Solving</p>
        </div>
        <p class="ib-theme-desc">This part of the course focuses more directly on designing solutions, writing programs, and using computational thinking to analyse and solve problems.</p>

        <div class="ib-unit-list">
            <a href="B1/index.html" class="ib-unit-card">
                <span class="ib-unit-code">B1</span>
                <div class="ib-unit-body">
                    <h3 class="ib-unit-name">Computational Thinking</h3>
                    <p class="ib-unit-desc">The ways computer scientists think about problems and solutions.</p>
                    <ul class="ib-subtopic-list">
                        <li>B1.1 Approaches to computational thinking</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <span class="ib-unit-hours">SL: 5h | HL: 5h</span>
            </a>

            <a href="B2/index.html" class="ib-unit-card">
                <span class="ib-unit-code">B2</span>
                <div class="ib-unit-body">
                    <h3 class="ib-unit-name">Programming</h3>
                    <p class="ib-unit-desc">The largest part of the course — practical programming knowledge needed to create working solutions.</p>
                    <ul class="ib-subtopic-list">
                        <li>B2.1 Programming fundamentals</li>
                        <li>B2.2 Data structures</li>
                        <li>B2.3 Programming constructs</li>
                        <li>B2.4 Programming algorithms</li>
                        <li>B2.5 File processing</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <span class="ib-unit-hours">SL: 40h | HL: 42h</span>
            </a>

            <a href="B3/index.html" class="ib-unit-card">
                <span class="ib-unit-code">B3</span>
                <div class="ib-unit-body">
                    <h3 class="ib-unit-name">Object-Oriented Programming</h3>
                    <p class="ib-unit-desc">Object-oriented design and programming.</p>
                    <ul class="ib-subtopic-list">
                        <li>B3.1 Fundamentals of OOP for a single class</li>
                        <li>B3.2 Fundamentals of OOP for multiple classes <span class="ib-hl-badge">HL</span></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <span class="ib-unit-hours">SL: 7h | HL: 23h</span>
            </a>

            <a href="B4/index.html" class="ib-unit-card">
                <span class="ib-unit-code">B4</span>
                <div class="ib-unit-body">
                    <h3 class="ib-unit-name">Abstract Data Types</h3>
                    <p class="ib-unit-desc">An additional HL-only unit covering linked lists, binary search trees, sets and hashing.</p>
                    <ul class="ib-subtopic-list">
                        <li>B4.1 Fundamentals of ADTs <span class="ib-hl-badge">HL</span></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <span class="ib-unit-hours">HL Only | 23h</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── Assessment ── #}
    <section class="ib-theme">
        <div class="ib-theme-header ib-theme-header--assess">
            <h2 class="ib-theme-label">Assessment</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="ib-theme-desc">The course is assessed through external examinations and one internal assessment task. At SL, external assessment makes up 70% of the final grade and the internal assessment makes up 30%. At HL, external assessment makes up 80% and the internal assessment makes up 20%.</p>

        <div class="ib-assess-grid">
            <div class="ib-assess-card">
                <h3 class="ib-assess-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-lines" aria-hidden="true"></i> Paper 1</h3>
                <p>Based on <strong>Theme A: Concepts of computer science</strong> and the pre-seen case study. Split into two sections.</p>
                <div class="ib-assess-levels">
                    <div class="ib-assess-level">
                        <span class="ib-assess-badge">SL</span>
                        <span>1h 15m — 35% of final grade</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ib-assess-level">
                        <span class="ib-assess-badge ib-assess-badge--hl">HL</span>
                        <span>2h — 40% of final grade</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <ul class="ib-assess-details">
                    <li><strong>Section A:</strong> Extended-response questions linked to Theme A</li>
                    <li><strong>Section B:</strong> Questions linked to the pre-seen case study</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="ib-assess-card">
                <h3 class="ib-assess-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-code" aria-hidden="true"></i> Paper 2</h3>
                <p>Based on <strong>Theme B: Computational thinking and problem-solving</strong>.</p>
                <div class="ib-assess-levels">
                    <div class="ib-assess-level">
                        <span class="ib-assess-badge">SL</span>
                        <span>1h 15m — 35%</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ib-assess-level">
                        <span class="ib-assess-badge ib-assess-badge--hl">HL</span>
                        <span>2h — 40%</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="ib-assess-note">Extended-response questions linked to Theme B. One SL question focuses on algorithmic thinking without requiring code.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="ib-assess-card">
                <h3 class="ib-assess-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-book-open" aria-hidden="true"></i> Case Study</h3>
                <p>A pre-seen scenario based on current developments, emerging technologies and/or ethical issues in computer science. Students research it in advance and answer questions in Paper 1 Section B.</p>
                <div class="ib-assess-levels">
                    <div class="ib-assess-level">
                        <span class="ib-assess-badge">SL</span>
                        <span>2 challenge questions</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ib-assess-level">
                        <span class="ib-assess-badge ib-assess-badge--hl">HL</span>
                        <span>4 challenge questions</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="ib-assess-note">Published 12 months before the May session or 18 months before the November session.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="ib-assess-card">
                <h3 class="ib-assess-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-laptop-code" aria-hidden="true"></i> Internal Assessment</h3>
                <p>The <strong>computational solution</strong> — a practical project where students identify a problem, develop a working computational solution, and document and evaluate what they have produced.</p>
                <div class="ib-assess-levels">
                    <div class="ib-assess-level">
                        <span class="ib-assess-badge">SL</span>
                        <span>30% of final grade</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ib-assess-level">
                        <span class="ib-assess-badge ib-assess-badge--hl">HL</span>
                        <span>20% of final grade</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="ib-assess-note">Internally assessed by the teacher, externally moderated by the IB.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="ib-assess-card">
                <h3 class="ib-assess-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-pen-fancy" aria-hidden="true"></i> Extended Essay</h3>
                <p>Computer Science can be chosen as an Extended Essay subject. The EE is an opportunity to carry out independent research — its emphasis is on research, analysis and argumentation, distinct from the practical IA.</p>
                <p class="ib-assess-note">Externally assessed. Optional.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── Summary ── #}
    <section class="ib-summary">
        <h2 class="ib-section-title">In Summary</h2>
        <p>IB Computer Science covers computer systems, networks, databases, machine learning, computational thinking, programming, object-oriented programming and, at HL, abstract data types and additional depth across several topics. Assessment is split between two exam papers and one practical internal assessment, with the case study forming a specific part of Paper 1 and the computational solution forming the IA.</p>
    </section>

</div>

